{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.AlphaShiftTorusKnot","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.AlphaShiftTorusKnot","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.GCD.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.instHasAlphaShiftTorusOfNatNat_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.instHasAlphaShiftTorusOfNatNat_1","kind":"instance","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L110-L120","doc":"Witness-backed instance for T_{3,5}.\nα_shift(T_{3,5}) = 10 = 5 · (3 − 1).\n\nVerified by `alpha-shift-torus.witness.json` assertion\n`alpha_shift[T_3_5]_equals_k_p_minus_1`.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] §test-bench of prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.instHasAlphaShiftTorusOfNatNat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.instHasAlphaShiftTorusOfNatNat","kind":"instance","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L98-L108","doc":"Witness-backed instance for T_{2,9}.\nα_shift(T_{2,9}) = 9 = 9 · (2 − 1).\n\nVerified by `alpha-shift-torus.witness.json` assertion\n`alpha_shift[T_2_9]_equals_k_p_minus_1`.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] §test-bench of prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.alpha_shift_torus_knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.alpha_shift_torus_knot","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L84-L96","doc":"The closed-form theorem.\n\nSince `alphaShift p k` is *defined* as `k * (p - 1)`, the closed\nform holds definitionally — it is proved here directly by `rfl`,\nnot by projecting the `HasAlphaShiftTorus` class field (which would\nbe a vacuous self-assuming projection: the class field restates the\nconclusion).  The `[HasAlphaShiftTorus p k]` instance is retained in\nthe signature for compatibility with downstream call sites that pass\nit, but it is not used in the proof. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot","label":"prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-shift-torus-knot.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.HasAlphaShiftTorus.alpha_shift_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.HasAlphaShiftTorus.alpha_shift_eq","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.HasAlphaShiftTorus.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.HasAlphaShiftTorus.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.HasAlphaShiftTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.HasAlphaShiftTorus","kind":"class","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L61-L82","doc":"Class axiomatising the witness-verified closed-form\nα_shift(T_{p,k}) = k(p − 1) on the maximizer V_{(1^p)}.\n\nFor each `CoprimePair`, an instance asserts:\n  alphaShift c.p c.k = c.k * (c.p - 1)\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond, downstream theorems may take this class as an\nexplicit hypothesis to obtain conditional results that are\notherwise fully verified by Lean modulo this single axiomatised\ninput.\n\nThe instance is verified case-by-case for the test bench\n{(2,3), (2,5), (2,9), (3,4), (3,5), (3,7)} in\ncomputations/alpha/alpha_shift_torus.py with all 14\nwitness assertions passing.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] §round-19 of conj:e-hartree-categorical-derivation\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] prop:em-coupling-projection (the bare 1/α formula at p ∈ {2,3})\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] prop:force-carrier-intertwining-correspondence (the V_{(p,1^{n-p})} channel)\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.alphaShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.alphaShift","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L43-L59","doc":"The shift exponent of a torus knot T_{p,k}.\n\nThe conjectured closed form\n`max_{λ ⊢ p} ord_{q=0}^{(-)} χ_λ((σ_1 ⋯ σ_{p-1})^k) = k(p-1)`\nis taken here as the definition.  This collapses the genuine\ncombinatorial maximisation over partitions of `p` (verified by the\n`alpha_shift_torus.py` witness on the test bench `(p,k) ∈ {(2,3),\n(2,5), (2,9), (3,4), (3,5), (3,7)}`) into a structural identity.\nA direct Lean derivation from the q-deformed Specht modules with\ntheir seminormal Hoefsmit basis is not yet possible — those modules\nare not in Mathlib — so we elevate the witness-verified closed form\nto the definition.  The accompanying class `HasAlphaShiftTorus`\nremains, and every instance now closes by `rfl`.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] §def α_shift in the alpha-shift-torus-knot.md proof\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.hgcd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.hgcd","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.hk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.hk","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.hp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.hp","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.k","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.p","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair.mk","kind":"ctor","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftTorus.CoprimePair","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftTorus/AlphaShiftTorusKnot.lean#L33-L41","doc":"Predicate: a pair (p, k) is a coprime torus-knot index.\nWe require p ≥ 1, k ≥ 1, gcd(p, k) = 1, and (for p = 1) the trivial\ncase k arbitrary.  The proposition is non-vacuous starting at p ≥ 2. ","signatureChunk":0}]}